1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:28,589
Chapter 14. Ebooks, audio, video, and download governance. Publication assets include the bilingual white paper, three EPUB interpretation ebooks, older Chinese and English audiobooks, lecture and MSI decks, MSI video, runnable source, and a download manifest. Every asset needs a version, language, purpose, and limitation.

2
00:00:28,909 --> 00:00:54,404
This guide bundles the white paper DOCX/PDF, three EPUBs, the 43.433-second MSI video, two PPTX decks, v0.2.0 source, and this guide's DOCX. Chapter audio, SRT/VTT, and transcripts are downloadable from the player.

3
00:00:54,724 --> 00:01:19,014
The EPUBs are audio-reading interpretations, not the full canon or substitutes for the white paper. Older audiobooks and this guide's narration are separate assets; never mix their captions or timelines. After replacing media, re-probe duration, streams, codecs, bytes, and SHA-256.

4
00:01:19,334 --> 00:01:42,109
The download manifest uses relative paths and rejects absolute paths, .., and symlink escapes. EPUB checks include mimetype, META-INF/container.xml, OPF manifest/spine, and XHTML anchors. A ZIP must be inspected beyond its header.

5
00:01:42,429 --> 00:01:51,237
Documents: white paper v1.1 and guide DOCX.

6
00:01:51,557 --> 00:02:00,774
Ebooks: Chinese, English, and bilingual EPUB.

7
00:02:01,094 --> 00:02:11,622
Media: 43.433-second MSI and per-chapter bilingual audio.

8
00:02:11,942 --> 00:02:22,239
Source and decks: v0.2.0 ZIP and two PPTX files.

9
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:37,201
Try one step: Open manifest.json, recompute SHA-256 and bytes for any three files, and inspect video and audio streams with ffprobe.
